/-!
# F2b′'s tail successor with the offset identity (D63)

Packet PROVE-T14-SB2LIFT (round 34, decisions D59 and D63). D63 adds the offset identity
`x₀ = Nc.entryRead (fill K) seed` to the successor statements (F3LAW consumes it for `hx₀le` through
`Fo.entryRead_eq_entry`). At a tail stage `ℓ` the seed is B's point `stPt (run ℓ)`, as in NOJUMP's construction
(`Nc.StageGoodAt.x0`).

* **`SB2LowerStageVersionStatement6E`**: CANON's `Cz.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement6` (D57), plus
  `∀ᵐ ω, ω ∈ F → x₀ ω = Nc.entryRead (fill (K ω)) (stPt (run ℓ))`, placed right after the entry clause (the
  layout of NOJUMP's root analogue `Ne.SB2LowerRootVersionStatement9E`);
* `sb2LowerStageVersionStatement6_of_6E`: its projection to Statement6.

R48: no source theorem is assumed; this is a named statement (proved in `SB2YjMain`:
`Sx.sb2LowerStageVersionStatement6E`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Set Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal
open QuantumZipper (H chiC fwdHull)
open LQGMetric (DistOn TestOn)

